        "original_id": "c16b4608-0d4e-5519-9c99-b85fd33277ac",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: Battle of White Plains, New York and New Jersey campaign\n- Places: White Plains, New York, New York City, New Jersey\n- People: General Sir William Howe, General George Washington\n- Topics: American Revolutionary War\n\nFacts:\n- The New York and New Jersey campaign was a series of battles for control of New York City and the state of New Jersey in the American Revolutionary War in 1776 and the winter months of 1777.\n- General Sir William Howe led the British forces in the New York and New Jersey campaign.\n- General George Washington led the Continental Army in the New York and New Jersey campaign.\n- The Battle of White Plains was fought near White Plains, New York, on October 28, 1776.\n- The Battle of White Plains was part of the New York and New Jersey campaign of the American Revolutionary War.",
